        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Heat, lignite briquette, at stove 5-15kW</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Heat, lignite briquette, at stove 5-15kW
The average net efficiency is 70 %. The stove is assumed to fire lignite briquettes. The heating value (19.5 MJ/kg) and the composition of the briquettes are average values available from the literature. The emission data are also taken from literature reporting measurements performed at the end of the 1980s in Germany. Size distribution of particles has been estimated on the basis of recent information from EPA. Emissions of trace elements  were calculated using the ash content in the coal and average transfer coefficients for coal power plants with ash retention of 98 %, as first approximation.;
UUID: 04990583-dc35-3812-b18b-22be1e0b628b
House heating. 
Location: German conditions.
Technology: Average used in early 1990s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography/Text
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_04990583-dc35-3812-b18b-22be1e0b628b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
